WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:56.000
Oil sands operations contribute significant carbon emissions in Canada. So the six largest companies have teamed up to make strides on the path to NetZero. Investing in technology and innovation. Already cut emissions in average 22% per barrel. Working with governments to create and protect jobs. Developing one of the world's largest carbon capture and storage facilities. Our NetZero plan is in motion and we're making progress on multiple pathways. See our plan in action at PathwaysAlliance.ca
加拿大油砂产业产生了大量碳排放，因此六家最大的公司携手合作，在迈向净零排放的道路上取得进展。投资于技术与 innovation。每桶排放量平均已减少22%。与政府合作创造和保护就业岗位。开发世界最大的碳捕集与储存设施之一。我们的净零计划正在实施中，我们正通过多种途径取得进展。请在PathwaysAlliance.ca查看我们的行动计划。

2
00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:52.000
For newlyweds Gail and Rick Brink, finding a dream home where they could settle down and start a family was at the top of their agenda. The couple met at work in 1984 when Gail was 19 years old and Rick was 25. With her long, wavy dark hair and athletic figure, Gail immediately caught Rick's attention. He knew right away that Gail was the one and told his mother later that day, I just met the woman I'm going to marry. Before long the pair were an item and were planning their wedding. On April 25, 1986, the day after Gail's 21st birthday, they were married in a simple church service in front of their closest friends and family.
对于新婚夫妇盖尔（Gail）和里克·布林克（Rick Brink）来说，寻找一个可以安家落户并组建家庭的梦想之家是他们首要任务。这对夫妇于1984年在工作中相识，当时盖尔19岁，里克25岁。盖尔留着长长的深色波浪卷发，身材健美，立刻引起了里克的注意。他一眼就看出盖尔就是他苦苦寻觅的另一半，并在那天晚些时候对母亲说，我刚遇到了我要娶的女人。不久之后，两人便确立了恋爱关系，并开始筹备婚礼。1986年4月25日，在盖尔21岁生日的第二天，他们在亲朋好友的见证下，于一家简朴的教堂举行了婚礼。

3
00:01:52.000 --> 00:02:32.000
Gail wore an elegant white dress with a flared skirt and spaghetti straps, while Rick wore a bright blue suit jacket and matching bow tie. The reception took place at a lakefront country club where guests danced all night long. After it was over, the bride and groom departed for their honeymoon, a romantic cruise where they would be able to spend lots of time on the beach soaking up sunshine. After Gail and Rick returned to their hometown of Holland, Michigan, they turned their attention to buying a house. One eventually caught their eye.
盖尔身穿优雅的白色连衣裙，裙摆外扩，带有细肩带，而里克则穿着一件亮蓝色西装外套和相配的领结。招待会在一家湖畔乡村俱乐部举行，宾客们通宵达旦地跳舞。仪式结束后，新郎新娘出发去度蜜月，那是一次浪漫的游轮之旅，他们将有大量时间在海滩上沐浴阳光。盖尔和里克回到家乡密歇根州荷兰镇后，便把注意力转向了买房。最终，有一处房子吸引了他们的目光。

4
00:02:32.000 --> 00:03:14.000
Located on the outskirts of town, it was a small weatherboard ranch house that sat on 20 acres of land. There was no doubt the property had seen better days. Inside, cabinets were falling off their hinges, paint was peeling, and the rooms were in desperate need of an upgrade. But it had great potential and Rick was confident he could turn it into their dream home. His job involved training carpenters at a furniture company and he was a talented handyman. With some help from his father, Rick negotiated a deal and was able to buy the house and land for a steal.
这栋房子位于镇郊，是一座小型木板平房，占地20英亩。毫无疑问，这处房产已经风光不再。走进屋内，橱柜脱落，墙漆剥落，各个房间急需翻新。但它具有巨大的潜力，里克有信心把它变成他们梦想中的家。他的工作涉及在一家家具公司培训木匠，而且他是个很有天赋的杂工。在父亲的帮助下，里克谈妥了一笔交易，以极低的价格买下了这栋房子和土地。

5
00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:49.000
After moving into the property in October 1987, the newlyweds set about transforming it. They went through the house room by room, scrubbing them from floor to ceiling, making repairs and repainting the walls. Rick documented their progress with the camcorder. He chatted about the house as he filmed each room and checked in on Gail, who paused her work to smile and wave at him. By November, the couple had been married for a year and a half and were ready to start renovating one room of their house in particular,
1987年10月搬进新居后，这对新婚夫妇便着手改造这所房子。他们逐个房间进行清洁，从地板到天花板进行擦洗，维修并重新粉刷了墙壁。里克用摄像机记录了他们的进展。他在拍摄每个房间时谈论着房子，并查看盖尔的情况，盖尔停下手里的活，向他微笑挥手。到了11月，这对夫妇已经结婚一年半了，准备开始装修他们房子的其中一个房间，

6
00:03:49.000 --> 00:04:54.000
a nursery, in preparation for the baby they hoped to have soon. Everything seemed to be going perfectly. Gail Brink had an office job at an auto parts company where she was well regarded as a diligent and hard working employee. So, when she didn't show up for work on the morning of Monday, November 23, her absence was immediately noticed. There was no sign of Rick at his workplace either. Knowing how responsible Rick was, his employer decided to check in with his family.
即育儿室，为他们希望不久后出生的宝宝做准备。一切似乎都在完美地进行。盖尔·布林克在一家汽车零部件公司做办公室文员，被认为是一个勤奋好学的员工。因此，当她在11月23日星期一早上没有去上班时，她的缺席立刻引起了注意。里克的公司也没有他的踪迹。深知里克是个多么有责任感的人，他的雇主决定向他的家人了解情况。

7
00:04:54.000 --> 00:05:30.000
Garrett and Ida Brink were surprised to receive a call informing them that their son hadn't been seen that day. Rick and Gail had attended a friend's wedding over the weekend, but they'd had no plans that would have kept them from work. Garrett and Ida decided to drive over to their house to check that everything was alright. When they arrived at the sprawling property north of Holland, Garrett and Ida noticed something. Rick's SUV, a Chevrolet Blazer, was parked in the driveway.
加勒特（Garrett）和艾达·布林克（Ida Brink）接到电话，得知他们的儿子那天没有去上班，感到很惊讶。里克和盖尔刚在周末参加了一个朋友的婚礼，但他们并没有什么会耽误工作的计划。加勒特和艾达决定开车去他们家看看一切是否安好。当他们到达荷兰镇北部的这处广阔房产时，加勒特和艾达注意到了一件事。里克的SUV雪佛兰开拓者停在车道上。

8
00:05:30.000 --> 00:06:07.000
That meant he must be at home. They went over to inspect the vehicle and saw something shocking. Rick was inside, slumped across the driver's seat with his head pressed against the passenger door. Blood was visible from at least one head wound. He was dead. When officers from the Ottawa County Sheriff's Department arrived, they secured the scene before walking into the home. Upon entering, they headed down the long hallway that led to the master bedroom.
这意味着他一定在家。他们走过去检查这辆车，看到了令人震惊的一幕。里克坐在车里，瘫倒在驾驶座上，头紧贴着乘客车门。至少有一处头部伤口清晰可见血迹。他已经死了。渥太华县治安官办公室的警员赶到后，在走进屋里之前封锁了现场。进入屋内后，他们顺着通往主卧室的长长走廊往前走。

9
00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:52.000
The room was tidy aside from some clothing that was strewn across the floor. Lying in the couple's water bed was 22-year-old Gail Brink. She looked as though she could be asleep, except for one thing. A blood-stained pillow had been placed over her head. When police lifted it, Gail's lifeless and bloody face was exposed. She had been shot in the head three times. Initially, officers wondered if they were dealing with a murder suicide. Perhaps Rick had killed his wife while she lay sleeping, then gone out into his Chevy Blazer to take his own life.
房间很整洁，除了地上散落的一些衣服。22岁的盖尔·布林克正躺在夫妻俩的水床上。她看起来就像是睡着了，除了有一点不同。一个沾满血迹的枕头盖在她的头上。警察掀开枕头，盖尔毫无生气且血迹斑斑的脸露了出来。她的头部被枪击了三次。起初，警员们怀疑这是一起谋杀后自杀案。也许里克在妻子熟睡时杀死了她，然后走到他的雪佛兰开拓者车里结束了自己的生命。

10
00:06:52.000 --> 00:07:36.000
But when investigators moved Rick's body, there was no gun lying beneath him. Nor was there one anywhere else in the car. Rick couldn't have been the killer. Like Gail, he'd been shot by someone else, execution style, with two bullet wounds in his head. Judging from the position of his body, he'd been sitting in the driver's seat when he was shot from the left side. Then he fell to the right, his head coming to rest on the passenger seat. The driver's side window was wound slightly down. A bullet hole through the passenger window had shattered the glass.
但是当调查人员移动里克的遗体时，他身下并没有枪。车里其他地方也没有枪。里克不可能是凶手。和盖尔一样，他是被其他人以行刑式枪决，头部有两处枪伤。从他尸体的位置来看，他坐在驾驶座上时从左侧遭到枪击。然后他向右倒下，头靠在乘客座上。驾驶座车窗稍微降下。乘客车窗上的一个弹孔击碎了玻璃。

11
00:07:36.000 --> 00:08:25.000
The killer had likely stood by the driver's door and aimed at the gun through the open window. Aside from the two victims and the few items of clothing lying on their bedroom floor, nothing in the house was out of place. There was no sign of forced entry. All of the furniture was upright and drawers were closed. Cash was found throughout the home. Gail's purse had been left on the kitchen counter, as had Rick's wallet. Both had all their contents, including credit cards and the driver's licenses. Gail and Rick were still wearing their wedding rings and other jewellery, and two watches were also found in the home.
凶手可能站在驾驶座车门旁，透过打开的车窗将枪对准了他。除了两名受害者和卧室地板上的几件衣服外，房子里的其他东西都井然有序。没有强行闯入的迹象。所有的家具都是直立的，抽屉都是关着的。房子里到处都能找到现金。盖尔的钱包被落在厨房柜台上，里克的钱包也是。两者的所有内容都完好无损，包括信用卡和驾照。盖尔和里克仍然戴着结婚戒指和其他首饰，屋里还找到了两块手表。

12
00:08:25.000 --> 00:09:08.000
Clearly, robbery hadn't been the killer's motive. The entire crime scene was unsettlingly clean, and there was little physical evidence to go on. Gail and Rick had both been shot with a 22 gauge revolver, but there was no sign of the murder weapon anywhere in the house. Nor were there any bullet casings. Detectives didn't recover any suspicious clothing or any strands of hair. Only six usable prints were recovered from the crime scene. Four fingerprints belonged to the two victims. Another print was found on a toilet, and there was also one on the telephone.
很明显，抢劫并不是凶手的动机。整个犯罪现场干净得令人不安，几乎没有什么物证可依。盖尔和里克都是被一把22口径左轮手枪射杀的，但屋里没有任何凶器的痕迹。也没有任何弹壳。侦探们没有找到任何可疑的衣服或任何头发。犯罪现场只提取到了六枚可用的指纹。四枚指纹属于两名受害者。另一个指纹在马桶上发现，还有一个在电话上。

13
00:09:08.000 --> 00:10:05.000
But these didn't match anyone in the police database. Faced with this dearth of physical evidence, detectives knew they would need to dig into the victim's lives. The last time anyone had seen Gail and Rick alive was on the night of Saturday, November 21, when they attended the wedding of one of Rick's high school friends. It seemed as though they had a good night. Rick had a few drinks, and Gail became rather tipsy before they left at around 11pm. The following day, Gail's brother, Ryan Winegarden, tried to call her at home, but there was no answer. Ryan had thought nothing of this at the time, but investigators speculated that the couple had been killed in the early hours of Sunday morning, after arriving home from the wedding.
但这些指纹与警方数据库中的任何人都不匹配。面对如此匮乏的物证，侦探们知道他们需要深入调查受害者的生活。任何人最后一次看到盖尔和里克活著是在11月21日星期六的晚上，当时他们参加了里克的一位高中朋友的婚礼。他们似乎度过了一个美好的夜晚。里克喝了几杯，盖尔在晚上11点左右离开前也有点微醉。第二天，盖尔的弟弟瑞安·温加顿（Ryan Winegarden）试图打电话给她，但无人接听。瑞安当时并没有多想，但调查人员推测这对夫妇是在星期天清晨从婚礼回家后被杀害的。

14
00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:59.000
The couple's family and friends were left in shock over the brutal slaying, with Ryan Winegarden telling local newspaper The Holland Sentinel, They were the nicest people in the world. I've never seen a couple get along better than they did. Gail had been one of eight children. Her family was close, but they struggled financially, which led to Gail dreaming of the day when she could finally be self-sufficient. She used to tell her big sister, Cheryl, how she planned to work as hard as she needed to, so she would always have enough money to buy herself whatever she wanted. Her first job was waitressing at a restaurant, where she earned excellent money despite the low wages. Gail was so funny, friendly and charming, that her customers always tipped generously.
这对夫妇的家人和朋友对这场残酷的谋杀案感到震惊，瑞安·温加顿对当地报纸《荷兰哨兵报》说：“他们是世界上最好的人。我从未见过比他们感情更好的情侣。”盖尔是八个孩子中的一个。她的家庭很亲密，但经济困难，这导致盖尔梦想着有一天能真正自立。她经常告诉姐姐谢丽尔（Cheryl），她计划尽其所能努力工作，以便永远有足够的钱给自己买任何想要的东西。她的第一份工作是在一家餐馆当服务员，尽管工资不高，但她赚了很多小费。盖尔是如此风趣、友好和迷人，以至于她的顾客总是慷慨地给小费。

15
00:10:59.000 --> 00:11:53.000
And when she met Rick, it seemed as though everything was falling into place. Not only were the young couple head over heels in love, but they were compatible too. Both were ambitious and didn't mind hard work. Their dream was a simple one, they wanted to raise a family and create a home where they could live for the rest of their lives. Rick swept Gail off her feet, spoiling her and giving her whatever she wanted. The young couple loved to travel, and during the summer months they would visit Rick's parents' house on the shores of Lake Michigan. Rick kept a boat out there and introduced Gail to water skiing. His friend Bill Whedon later told the television program a wedding and a murder that Gail was like liquid sunshine to Rick.
当她遇到里克时，一切似乎都水到渠成。这对年轻夫妇不仅深陷爱河，而且十分契合。两人都雄心勃勃，并不介意辛苦工作。他们的梦想很简单，就是抚养一个家庭，创造一个可以度过余生的家。里克对盖尔一见倾心，对她百般溺爱，要什么给什么。这对年轻夫妇喜欢旅行，夏天的时候他们会去里克父母位于密歇根湖畔的房子。里克在那里存了一艘船，并教会了盖尔滑水。他的朋友比尔·惠顿（Bill Whedon）后来告诉电视节目《婚礼与谋杀案》，对里克来说，盖尔就像流动的阳光。

16
00:11:53.000 --> 00:12:43.000
She was the kind of person who could light up a room just by entering it. But despite the idyllic life the pair had together, the beginning of their relationship hadn't exactly been smooth sailing. Prior to meeting Rick, Gail had another serious boyfriend named Lars. She'd moved in with him when she was 18 years old and they'd built a house together. They'd been living together for about a year when Gail met Rick at work. She quickly ended her relationship so she could be with Rick, but Lars didn't take the news well. As she was packing her belongings to move out, he slammed a drawer closed on her hand. He also hit Gail, giving her a black eye.
她是那种只要走进房间就能点亮整个房间的人。然而，尽管两人有着田园诗般的生活，但他们的恋爱关系的开始并非一帆风顺。在遇到里克之前，盖尔还有另一个认真的男朋友，名叫拉尔斯（Lars）。她18岁时就搬去跟他一起住，两人还一起建了一栋房子。他们同居大约一年后，盖尔在工作中遇到了里克。她迅速结束了这段感情以便和里克在一起，但拉尔斯对这个消息反应激烈。当她打包行李准备搬走时，他把抽屉猛地关在她的手上。他还打了盖尔，把她的眼睛打青了。

17
00:12:43.000 --> 00:13:32.000
After hearing about the assault, Gail's protective big brother Ryan came to her rescue. He punched Lars, breaking his nose, then warned him, Don't you touch my sister again. When police started looking for a suspect, Ryan suggested they speak with Gail's ex-boyfriend. He believed Lars was still in love with Gail and was furious that she'd married someone else. Investigators quickly tracked Lars down. He admitted to assaulting Gail, but strongly denied having anything to do with the double homicide. When detectives asked if he would be willing to sit a polygraph test, Lars agreed.
听说袭击事件后，盖尔富有保护欲的大哥瑞安赶来解救她。他打了拉尔斯，打断了他的鼻子，然后警告他：“你再敢碰我妹妹一下试试。”当警方开始寻找嫌疑人时，瑞安建议他们找盖尔的前男友谈谈。他相信拉尔斯仍然爱着盖尔，并且对她嫁给别人感到愤怒。调查人员很快找到了拉尔斯。他承认袭击了盖尔，但坚决否认与这起双重谋杀案有任何关系。当侦探询问他是否愿意接受测谎仪测试时，拉尔斯同意了。

18
00:13:32.000 --> 00:14:19.000
He passed the test. He also provided an alibi for the time of the murders. It checked out and Lars was dismissed as a suspect. Investigators went back to the drawing board. Gail and Rick Brink were farewell in a joint funeral and laid to rest in a shared plot. The detectives working the case spoke extensively with the couple's friends and family, but nobody raised any red flags. They even tracked down every person who'd been a guest at the wedding the couple attended on their last night alive. They couldn't find anyone who held a grudge against the young newlyweds.
他通过了测试。他还为谋杀发生的时间提供了不在场证明。经过核实，拉尔斯被排除嫌疑。调查人员重新回到起点。盖尔和里克·布林克在一次联合葬礼上告别，并安葬在同一个墓地里。负责此案的侦探与这对夫妇的朋友和家人进行了广泛的交谈，但没有人提出任何可疑之处。他们甚至找到了这对夫妇生命中最后一晚参加婚礼的所有宾客。他们找不到任何人对这对年轻夫妇怀恨在心。

19
00:14:19.000 --> 00:15:18.000
They had no criminal histories or connections whatsoever. By all accounts, they were well-liked, upstanding citizens who'd had no bad blood with anybody. In fact, there was only one thing in their lives that seemed it could be the source of some tension. They're newly acquired home. The ranch house sat on the eerily named Ransom Street and before the couple had bought it, had belonged to a bikey who went by the nickname Shotgun Sid. Sid was a somewhat notorious figure throughout Michigan's criminal circles. He trafficked illicit drugs from the city of Detroit to the western part of the state for a bikey gang named the Highwaymen. But Sid grew disturbed after he saw dealers selling drugs to teenagers at local high schools.
他们没有任何犯罪记录或任何联系。据所有人所说，他们是深受欢迎、奉公守法的公民，与任何人都没有宿怨。事实上，他们生活中似乎只有一件事可能是某些紧张关系的根源。他们新买的房子。这栋牧场风格的房子位于一个有着诡异名字的“ランサム街”（Ransom Street），在这对夫妇买下它之前，它属于一个绰号叫“霰弹枪西德”（Shotgun Sid）的飞车党。西德在密歇根州的犯罪圈子里是个相当臭名昭著的人物。他为一个名为“高速公路人”（Highwaymen）的飞车党从底特律市向该州西部贩运非法毒品。但西德看到毒贩向当地高中的青少年出售毒品后感到不安。

20
00:15:18.000 --> 00:16:14.000
He began a double life as an informant, providing federal agents with the names of individuals who were selling to children. When word got out that Sid was working with the authorities, his life was threatened. He was shot at on multiple occasions. One time, three people turned up with a shotgun at his Ransom Street address. Sid pulled out a firearm of his own and convinced the intruders to drop their weapon. It later turned out that these individuals had been looking for a car that Sid was holding as collateral for a drug debt. In addition to enduring physical threats, Shotgun Sid was struggling financially and failed to make the repayments on his house. Eventually, the bank foreclosed on his mortgage and Sid was forced to vacate the property.
他开始了双重生活，成为一名线人，向联邦特工提供向儿童贩毒的人的名单。当西德与当局合作的消息传出后，他的生命受到了威胁。他多次遭到枪击。有一次，三个人带着一把霰弹枪出现在他的兰瑟姆街住址。西德掏出自己的枪，说服闯入者放下武器。后来证明，这些人一直在寻找西德作为毒债抵押品扣押的一辆车。除了忍受人身威胁外，“霰弹枪西德”还面临着经济困难，无力偿还房屋贷款。最终，银行没收了他的抵押贷款，西德被迫腾出这处房产。

21
00:16:14.000 --> 00:17:04.000
